    ],
    "basis": "Seligman & Seligman 1932, p.37: limits stated in the text only. Quote: The Shilluk country forms a narrow fringe on the west bank of the Nile, from Kaka in the north to within 30 miles of Lake No in the south. From Kodok to Taufikia the Shilluk also occupy the east bank, and their villages extend some 35 miles up the Sobat River, principally on the north bank.",
    "method": "Text-limit redraw. Only the limits stated on p.37 are used; no coordinate is invented. Named places from Wikidata P625. Rivers: Natural Earth 10m rivers/lake centrelines (White Nile, Bahr el Jebel, Sobat, Akobo); Baro: OpenStreetMap ways (ODbL). Projection for distances: local equirectangular at 9°N. Bank bands are 10 km each side or on the stated bank (EDITORIAL width; the pages give banks, not widths).",
